# LANE lds (feature/log-distance-score 9db8d58): score = temp * -log(dist(p_u, p_v)). Optimiser: SparseAdam on E (master's), Adam on the head.
#   --lr 1e-3 (head) and --lr-embedding 1e-4 (E), branch defaults, nothing on the cmd line.
# THE PAIR. lds and ald carry the SAME scorer and differ ONLY in the optimiser on E:
#   lds = master 16cedd9 + the log line, so SparseAdam (lazy v: an absent row's second
#         moment is untouched, so a returning row steps at exactly lr).
#   ald = the same log line on dense Adam with beta1 = 0, where v decays on wall-clock
#         steps. With a row touched every k steps v settles at g^2/k, so sqrt(v_hat) ~
#         |g|/sqrt(k) and EVERY row's step is inflated by ~sqrt(k). MEASURED on tgbl-coin:
#         5,932 distinct rows per step of 638,486 -> k = 108, and the probe read
#         g_rms 3.785e-05 against sqvh 4.210e-06, a ratio of 9.0 against the predicted 10.4.
# WHY REVIEW. k = N_rows / rows-touched-per-step is the dataset variable, and review is the
#   SMALLEST table in the suite (352,637 rows, 4.87M edges) -- it should sit at a LOWER k
#   than coin (108) and comment (~166), so a SMALLER lds-over-ald margin is the prediction.
#   It is also the one dataset that overfits inside ~2 epochs (every lane here selects ep1-2
#   of 11-12), so it tests the scorer where there is almost no training to optimise.
# READ r_max BEFORE THE MRR. log(c*d) = log c + log d and the -temp*log c term is identical
#   for every candidate in a query, so it cancels in the softmax: the LOSS is exactly
#   degree-0 homogeneous in E and <E, grad_E L> = 0. The radial direction carries NO
#   gradient and nothing restrains it. On logs/lds_9db8d58 (coin) r_max grows a linear
#   +0.21/epoch while r_mean stays flat at 1.13. A run whose r_max climbs linearly while
#   val is flat can be stopped.
# NOT AN EXPRESSIVENESS TEST: at fixed weights -temp*log d is strictly monotone in d, so it
#   induces exactly master's ranking and master's MRR. Every difference is optimisation.
# REFERENCES on tgbl-review -- READ THE CAVEAT. There is NO current-era master number here: no run
#   at 6e50b71 (N(0,1/d) init) or later has covered tgbl-review, and the fc pair
#   (SparseAdam vs dense Adam b1=0) was coin/comment/flight only. So the ONLY clean
#   contrast in this cell is lds vs ald. The nearest numbers, all PRE-init-change and
#   therefore NOT comparable in absolute terms:
#     master 633a5a0 raw dist, one Adam lr1e-3:      0.1463 (max 0.1464, sel 2/12)
#     log-dist 0502d88, one dense Adam lr1e-3:       0.1564 (max 0.1564, sel 2/12),
#       i.e. the log scorer was worth +0.0101 there, and its r_max ran 1.75 -> 8.15 over
#       12 epochs while val fell every epoch after ep2 -- the degree-0 signature.
#     mean-rescale 7e58033 (r_mean pinned to 1):     0.1819 (max 0.1819, sel 1/11)
